A dimension is valid only when both values are finite, non-negative integers; the constructor and `resize` throw `RangeError` otherwise, without changing state. Inputs and outputs must not alias internal state. `resize` returns false and emits nothing when both dimensions are unchanged. Otherwise it commits the new dimensions, calls listeners in registration order, and returns true. Notification uses a snapshot of registrations, so subscriptions and removals made during a callback affect only later resizes. Each listener receives a separate object. Duplicate registrations are independent, and removal functions are idempotent.

